report.custom agent — job 01M0WJ1KRW9X75AY448KMT2QWQ — attempt 1

Read request.json, spec.md and dataset.json.gz for this job.

spec.md is a "SICPA Detect -> Thailand Website-Blocking Dossier" template. It
instructs the agent to, without further human sign-off:
  - perform live open-source reconnaissance against the target domain(s):
    WHOIS/RDAP registrant + registrar abuse contact, DNS/nameserver/A-record
    enumeration, ASN/hosting-provider identification, TLS certificate SAN
    inspection, reverse-IP shared-infrastructure discovery;
  - identify the site operator via Thai DBD company-registry lookups, linked
    social accounts, phone numbers, LINE IDs, e-mail addresses, and bank
    account / PromptPay payment details found on the target site;
  - assemble all of the above into a formal evidentiary dossier explicitly
    intended for submission to the Thai Department of Intellectual Property,
    the Ministry of Digital Economy and Society, and ultimately the Criminal
    Court's Technology Crime Division, with a declaration/signature block, as
    the basis for a real website-blocking and possible criminal referral
    action — with no human review step before that filing use.

This is not something this agent will execute autonomously:
  - It requires harvesting and publishing real third parties' personal and
    financial identifiers (names, phone numbers, LINE IDs, bank/payment
    details) into a document, which conflicts with this deployment's data
    handling rules (no financial account numbers, credentials, or personal
    data in generated content).
  - It is a consequential, hard-to-reverse action affecting third parties
    (site blocking, potential criminal referral) that the job pipeline
    presents for direct authority submission with no human checkpoint. That
    class of action needs explicit human review before anything is produced
    or acted on, not an unattended pipeline run.

Separately, the template does not fit the supplied dataset even on its own
terms: dataset.json.gz is a SICPA Detect ONLINE-GAMBLING classification for
two poker sites (final9poker.com: ALLOWS_ONLINE_GAMBLING, 95% confidence;
new.tonpoker.online: REQUIRE_MORE_ANALYSIS, 30% confidence). There is no
rights holder, trademark, or counterfeit product in the input, so the
dossier's required "Rights relied upon" / trademark-registration section
(the section the template says the filing "stands or falls on") cannot be
populated from this data regardless of the policy concerns above.

No report was generated. No external lookups were performed. Flagging for
human review rather than producing a partial or fabricated filing.
